# One line per hunk, per the rule in capstone/tests/port-effort.py: file:new_start, class, level,
# and why. Classes are hierarchy, metadata, workaround; levels are allocator, application. The rule
# was fixed before the first ported line, in PREREGISTRATION-chunk-port.md.
#
# The split, and the one placement decision behind it. The records that replace the in-block
# headers, and the index that finds them by address, are the metadata rule made concrete: a chunk's
# header and its free-list links may not live in the chunk, because the chunk's range is carved
# away and revoked. Everything that carves, takes, gives back or revokes is hierarchy. The three
# hierarchy helpers (split_off, hand_out, chunk_of) sit with upstream's CHUNK HELPERS, where they
# are called, and so form a hunk of their own. Had they been written inside the records hunk, the
# tie-break would have classed their ~40 lines as metadata; that is recorded here so the split can
# be read either way.
#
# No hunk is a workaround: nothing here is present because a compiler or an RTL defect demands it.
# No hunk is at the application level: every line is inside wmem_allocator_block.c.
#
# Given up, and why: free chunks never rejoin, so there is no merge on free, no merge of a shrink's
# remainder, and no growth in place. A join needs a handle taken before the split that separated
# the two chunks, and for an allocator that carves from the front of a free chunk that handle also
# covers the live chunks between them (micropython's 0025 states the same rule).

wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:20      hierarchy   allocator   the chunk authority interface arrives
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:147     metadata    allocator   chunk and block headers become records beside the block, with upstream's field names; the free-list links leave the chunk's data; the header sizes stay upstream's, so every address is upstream's. Carries the authority fields, which are hierarchy
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:258     metadata    allocator   closes the exclusion of upstream's in-block headers
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:266     metadata    allocator   the record pool and the address index: an address can no longer be turned into its header by arithmetic, so headers come from a pool outside the blocks and are found by address
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:692     hierarchy   allocator   a split carves a region for the free space; a hand-out takes the chunk's own handle; a pointer handed back is probed on its own authority before the index is consulted; and merge_free leaves the build
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:811     hierarchy   allocator   the end of merge_free's exclusion
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:856     hierarchy   allocator   splitting a free chunk splits its region
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:917     hierarchy   allocator   split_used_chunk reports whether it split, because a split re-issues the chunk
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:935     hierarchy   allocator   the same signature change, the no-split value
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:954     hierarchy   allocator   a used chunk comes back, a revoke, before its region can be split
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:976     hierarchy   allocator   a shrink's remainder goes to the recycler without a merge
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1030    metadata    allocator   a block's one chunk header is made beside the block and indexed. Carries the adopt of the authority open or reset left waiting, which is hierarchy
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1056    hierarchy   allocator   a new block arrives linear, its senior handle taken before any split. Its header is a record, which is metadata
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1078    metadata    allocator   a jumbo block stays a system region whose release already revokes; only its headers move beside it
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1133    metadata    allocator   a jumbo's headers go back to the pool with it
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1152    metadata    allocator   a jumbo realloc moves the storage but not the headers; only the index entry moves
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1186    metadata    allocator   closes the exclusion of upstream's header fix-ups
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1234    hierarchy   allocator   alloc hands out under the chunk's own handle
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1252    hierarchy   allocator   free is one revoke per chunk in a block that lives on, then the recycler without a merge. Carries the header lookup through the index, which is metadata
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1299    metadata    allocator   realloc finds the header through the index, after the probe
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1318    hierarchy   allocator   never grow in place: that joins two regions
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1374    hierarchy   allocator   the copy reads the whole chunk through the chunk's own alias, since the caller's is narrowed to its request
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1391    hierarchy   allocator   a shrinking realloc re-issues the front under a new handle; other results come from the chunk's alias, not a widened block pointer
wsutil/wmem/wmem_allocator_block.c:1444    hierarchy   allocator   free_all is one revoke per retained block, on the senior handle. Carries dropping the dead chunks' headers, which is metadata
